{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788059238805187001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"crucial-petaline-antbear","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"81a1958be38dd6c910a5064c629c02e7265e00d2738f59a988678e95e1ebf6b4","event_uuid":"2cdfe9ec-0115-4318-b152-9d98e71f3574","position":{"commit_sha":"b2af319453e1d4b65d9d3bfcdd2e0d24fea92694","position":"1788056654204157913-2cdfe9ec-0115-4318-b152-9d98e71f3574"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"95e99ceeff68e462ebe5ef82f6f5f3af59659cb5dd21103b79a89816c898c26c","event_uuid":"03059892-ae2d-4018-b6ac-141e2fd9b2f6","position":{"commit_sha":"38df52c9a197ad6049e294d615c501415bc6b5db","position":"1788056972582380283-03059892-ae2d-4018-b6ac-141e2fd9b2f6"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## Refined-bar reinforcement (stays READY-TO-FIX; sharpened recommendation)\n\nThe refined standard confirms this as the ROOT correction and clarifies the target code. **Do NOT split into several narrow codes.** The one honest principle for branch 6:\n\n- Keep `llm_unavailable` for `isinstance(exc, LLMUnavailableError)` (incl. LLMConfigError) — its scenario set (extra absent, credentials missing/invalid, provider unreachable/rate-limited/refused) accurately fits the name.\n- Everything else under `LLMError` → `command_failed`, the existing broad-but-accurate \"an unclassified rebar command failure.\" That code honestly covers the whole residual set (input rejections, tool-loop/budget self-stops, context-window, output defects, and — pending 73d8 — workflow/expression faults) WITHOUT naming a wrong cause.\n\n**Why `command_failed` and not new vocab:** per the 35ab/551b precedent, grow vocabulary only for demonstrated observable need. `command_failed` is not misleading for these scenarios — it makes no false cause claim — so it is an accurate fit, just broad. Finer per-type codes (input_rejected, output_invalid, …) are OPTIONAL and should be filed separately only if a consumer needs the distinction.\n\nImplementation note: narrowing branch 6 to `LLMUnavailableError` is the single change that also fixes 7d47 (load-time WorkflowError) and resolves the 73d8/551b tension (a genuine execute-time outage is an `LLMUnavailableError` and stays `llm_unavailable`; an `ExpressionError` is not, so it correctly falls to `command_failed`).","timestamp":1788056972582380283}],"created_at":1788056654204157913,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[],"description":"## Finding (audit of epic 3405-c0b7)\n**Site:** the gate degrade producers in `src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py` — `_degraded_plan_review_verdict` (via the `except (LLMUnavailableError, LLMInputRejectedError)` arm at line 203), `_degraded_code_review_verdict` (line ~336 sets `\"llm_unavailable\": True`), and the completion-verdict degrade. They emit `coverage.llm_unavailable = True`.\n\n**Problem:** the arm catches `(LLMUnavailableError, LLMInputRejectedError)` together (comment at line 203 folds `LLMInputRejectedError`, bug 43d4, into \"the mid-run infra outage\" arm). So when the cause is an INPUT REJECTION (oversized/malformed prompt, content-policy refusal), the verdict still carries `coverage.llm_unavailable=True`. The field's docstring admits the name is overloaded to mean \"no provider record accompanies this verdict\" (degraded), NOT literally \"the provider is down\".\n\n**Wrong signal:** `coverage.llm_unavailable=True` for a non-availability fault. `resolution_fields(outcome)` DOES ride the truthful `resolution_class` (CHANGE_INPUT) alongside, so the disposition is recoverable — but the boolean's NAME misreports the cause.\n\n**Consumers that branch on the boolean:** `plan_review/drift_floor.py:202`, `plan_review/orchestrator.py:468`, `review_bot/adapter.py:114`.\n\n**Observable vs latent:** OBSERVABLE — on every degraded gate verdict JSON and to the three consumers above.\n\n**Proposed fix (needs decision):** behavior-change / rename — either split the flag (a neutral `degraded` / `no_provider_record` boolean vs a strict `llm_unavailable` reserved for real outages) or have consumers/readers key off `resolution_class` instead of the overloaded boolean. Affects the verdict contract and three consumers → **escalate**.\n\n**caused_by / class:** the same \"input-rejection framed as provider outage\" pattern; origin 8a31 / bug 43d4.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["parent","3405-c0b7-0436-4b46"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"3405-c0b7-0436-4b46","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["error-taxonomy","escalate","observable"],"ticket_id":"5f96-25aa-af9d-4f57","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Gate degrade sets coverage.llm_unavailable=True for LLMInputRejectedError (overloaded/misleading boolean)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["2cdfe9ec-0115-4318-b152-9d98e71f3574","03059892-ae2d-4018-b6ac-141e2fd9b2f6"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788059238805187001,"uuid":"dacc0616-d11f-4413-ae4f-7015b653d668"}